    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for PT-141 (Bremelanotide)."
  },
  "peptideContentPt141Notes": "일부 시장에서는 처방 의약품입니다. 정기 일정이 아니라 필요 시 사용하는 방식으로 승인되었습니다. 흔한 부작용으로 메스꺼움과 일시적인 혈압 상승이 보고됩니다.",
  "@peptideContentPt141Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Prescription medication in some markets. Taken as needed rather than on a fixed schedule. Common side effects include nausea and transient blood pressure increases.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipDescription": "델타 수면 유도 펩타이드(DSIP)는 1970년대 토끼 뇌에서 분리된 노나펩타이드입니다. 수면 조절, 통증 조절 및 스트레스 반응에서의 가능성을 연구했지만, 작용 기전은 아직 명확하지 않습니다.",
  "@peptideContentDsipDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for DSIP.",
    "sourceString": "Delta Sleep-Inducing Peptide (DSIP) is a nonapeptide isolated from rabbit brain in the 1970s. It has been studied for possible roles in sleep regulation, pain modulation, and stress response, though mechanisms remain unclear.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for DSIP."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipTypicalDose": "잠자리에 들기 전 100~500mcg",
  "@peptideContentDsipTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for DSIP; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–500 mcg before bed",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for DSIP; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipHalfLife": "~7분",
  "@peptideContentDsipHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for DSIP.",
    "sourceString": "~7 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for DSIP."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipNotes": "일반적으로 잠자리에 들기 전에 투여합니다. 혈장 반감기는 짧지만 보고된 효과는 반감기보다 오래 지속될 수 있습니다. 증거 기반은 여전히 ​​제한적입니다.",
  "@peptideContentDsipNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for DSIP; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Typically administered before bed. Short plasma half-life but reported effects may outlast it. Evidence base remains limited.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for DSIP; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Description": "티모신 알파-1(Thymosin Alpha-1)은 원래 흉선 조직에서 분리된 28개 아미노산 펩타이드입니다. 이 제품은 B형 및 C형 간염에 대한 보조 면역 조절 치료제(상표명 Zadaxin)로 여러 국가에서 승인되었습니다.",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Thymosin Alpha-1.",
    "sourceString": "Thymosin Alpha-1 is a 28-amino-acid peptide originally isolated from thymus tissue. It has been approved in multiple countries as an adjunct immune-modulating therapy (brand name Zadaxin) for hepatitis B and C.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Thymosin Alpha-1."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1TypicalDose": "1.6mg을 주 2회",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Thymosin Alpha-1; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "1.6 mg twice weekly",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Thymosin Alpha-1; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1HalfLife": "~2시간",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Thymosin Alpha-1.",
    "sourceString": "~2 hours",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Thymosin Alpha-1."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Notes": "면역 조절 프로토콜의 일부로 여러 국제 시장에서 사용됩니다. 일반적으로 주 2회 투여됩니다. 다양한 적응증에 대한 연구가 계속되고 있습니다.",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Thymosin Alpha-1; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Used in several international markets as part of immune-modulation protocols. Typically administered twice weekly. Research continues in various indications.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Thymosin Alpha-1; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusDescription": "NAD+(니코틴아미드 아데닌 디뉴클레오티드)는 세포 에너지 대사와 DNA 복구에 핵심적인 보조효소입니다. 주사 가능한 NAD+ 및 그 전구체(NR, NMN)는 미토콘드리아 건강 및 노화와 관련하여 연구됩니다.",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for NAD+.",
    "sourceString": "NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is a coenzyme central to cellular energy metabolism and DNA repair. Injectable NAD+ and its precursors (NR, NMN) are studied in the context of mitochondrial health and ageing.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for NAD+."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusTypicalDose": "세션당 100~500mg IV 또는 SubQ",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for NAD+; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–500 mg IV or SubQ per session",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for NAD+; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusHalfLife": "~90분",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for NAD+.",
    "sourceString": "~90 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for NAD+."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusNotes": "엄밀히는 펩타이드가 아닌 조효소지만 장수 관련 프로토콜과 함께 다뤄지기도 합니다. 홍조와 불편감과의 관련성 때문에 느린 주입 방식이 언급됩니다.",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for NAD+; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Technically a coenzyme rather than a peptide, but commonly grouped with longevity protocols. Slow infusion is recommended to minimise flushing and discomfort.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for NAD+; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinDescription": "Sermorelin은 성장 호르몬 방출 호르몬(GHRH)의 합성 유사체입니다. 이는 성장 호르몬 보유를 위한 진단제로 임상적으로 사용되어 왔으며 웰니스 환경에서 GH축 지지 펩타이드로 흔히 논의됩니다.",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Sermorelin.",
    "sourceString": "Sermorelin is a synthetic analogue of growth hormone-releasing hormone (GHRH). It has been used clinically as a diagnostic agent for growth-hormone reserve and is commonly discussed in wellness settings as a GH-axis support peptide.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Sermorelin."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinTypicalDose": "잠자리에 들기 전 100~300mcg",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Sermorelin; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–300 mcg before bed",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Sermorelin; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinHalfLife": "~10~20분",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Sermorelin.",
    "sourceString": "~10–20 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Sermorelin."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinNotes": "둘 다 GHRH 경로에 작용하기 때문에 CJC-1295 no-DAC와 종종 비교됩니다. 짧은 반감기로 인해 비임상 프로토콜에서는 저녁 투여가 일반적입니다.",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Sermorelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Often compared with CJC-1295 no-DAC because both act on the GHRH pathway. Short half-life makes evening dosing common in non-clinical protocols.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Sermorelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentAod9604Description": "AOD-9604는 176-191 영역에서 파생된 인간 성장 호르몬의 변형된 단편입니다. 대사 및 지방 분해 신호 전달에 대해 조사되었지만 공개된 인간 증거는 제한적이고 혼합되어 있습니다.",
  "@peptideContentAod9604Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for AOD-9604.",
    "sourceString": "AOD-9604 is a modified fragment of human growth hormone, derived from the 176–191 region. It has been investigated for metabolic and lipolysis signalling, but published human evidence is limited and mixed.",
